"b2805a84-82bd-45d1-ba68-db82cc33368e (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/adminorderac01-22.pdf)\nciteturn1024view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn997view0\",\"id\":332}); Total lines: 17\nL0@P0: Superior Court of California\nL1@P0: County of Orange\nL2@P0: Chambers of\nL3@P0: LAYNE H. MELZER 700 CIVIC CENTER DRIVE WEST\nL4@P0: CIVIL SUPERVISING JUDGE SANTA ANA, CA 92701\nL5@P0: 657-622-5212\nL6@P0: ADMINISTRATIVE CIVIL ORDER: AC 01/22\nL7@P0: SMALL CLAIMS ELECTRONIC EVIDENCE\nL8@P0: In April 2021, the Superior Court of California, County of Orange successfully piloted a project for use of an\nL9@P0: electronic evidence portal in designated courtrooms. The electronic evidence portal was used in small claims\nL10@P0: courtrooms to promote greater access to justice, promote court efficiency, enhance evidence management\nL11@P0: practice, and facilitate remote hearings.\nL12@P0: For small claims cases heard between April 5, 2021 to March 6, 2022, documents uploaded by the parties to the\nL13@P0: electronic evidence portal remain in the portal. | hereby order that any exhibits uploaded to the electronic\nL14@P0: evidence portal for small claims proceedings which were concluded between April 5, 2021 through March 6,\nL15@P0: 2022 to be purged from the portal 30 days from the date of this order. Parties who wish to retain copies have\nL16@P0: 30 days from the date of this order to log into the portal to download any previously uploaded exhibits.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMicrosoft Word - Small_Claims_and_Appearance_Information (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/civil/appearanceprocedureandinformationsmallclaims.pdf)\nciteturn1024view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn997view0\",\"id\":319}); Total lines: 37\nL0@P0: 1 | P a g e\nL1@P0: Superior Court of California\nL2@P0: County of Orange\nL3@P0: Appearance Procedure and Information\nL4@P0: Civil - Small Claims\nL5@P0: UPDATE – June 30, 2025\nL6@P0: In-person services are available in the Civil Clerk’s Office Monday through Friday from 8:00 a.m. to 4:00\nL7@P0: p.m.\nL8@P0: 1. Filings: Filings may be submitted in-person at the Central Justice Center, via eFiling through an\nL9@P0: approved eFiling Service Provider, or by US Mail at 700 Civic Center Drive West, Santa Ana, CA\nL10@P0: 92701.\nL11@P0: 2. Questions: Specific questions can be submitted via the “Ask a Question” button on the court’s\nL12@P0: website.\nL13@P0: 3. Self Help Assistance: The public is encouraged to consult Self Help Services prior to filing\nL14@P0: documents. To contact Self Help, visit www.occourts.org/self-help and select \"Click Here to Contact\nL15@P0: Self Help Services.”\nL16@P0: 4. Appearances: (Department C16)\nL17@P0: Unless the court orders otherwise, all Small Claims trials will initially be set for a remote evidentiary\nL18@P0: hearing to assess notice, opposition, trial readiness, technical capabilities to conduct a remote small\nL19@P0: claims trial, and to hear default prove-ups. Contested Small Claims trials will take place at a later\nL20@P0: date. A party choosing to appear in person can do so by appearing in the courtroom on the\nL21@P0: date/time of the initial appearance. Notice of the mode of appearance for the Small Claims trial is to\nL22@P0: be given at the initial appearance. Any opposition to remote appearance will be considered by the\nL23@P0: court at the initial appearance.\nL24@P0: Remote appearance will be conducted via Zoom through the video links available on the court’s\nL25@P0: public website at https://www.occourts.org, Civil Division, Civil Appearance Procedure and\nL26@P0: Information page, and locate the blue banner below, then scroll down to Department C16 under\nL27@P0: Central Justice Center. Or click on the blue banner below.\nL28@P0: Parties are encouraged to appear for the initial trial hearing by video for your convenience. To\nL29@P0: view Remote Hearing Instructions click here or visit https://www.occourts.org/general-information/\nL30@P0: remote-appearance-information.\nL31@P0: In the event a party, witness, official reporter, official reporter pro tempore, court interpreter, or\nL32@P0: other court personnel experiences technology or audibility issues that arise during a remote\nL33@P0: conference, hearing, proceeding, or trial, the person is to alert the court by calling the courtroom\nL34@P0: clerk for Department C16 at (657) 622–5216.\nL35@P0: Parties should review Local Rule 375 for additional appearance information.\nL36@P0: 5. Small Claims Appeals: Hearings will continue to be heard in-person as noticed by the court.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMicrosoft Word - Evictions_(UD)_Information_and_Video_Appearance_Process (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/civil/evictions_ud_appearance_procedure_and_information_09_2024.pdf)\nciteturn1024view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn997view0\",\"id\":320}); Total lines: 32\nL0@P0: 1 | P a g e\nL1@P0: Superior Court of California\nL2@P0: County of Orange\nL3@P0: Appearance Procedure and Information\nL4@P0: Civil - Unlawful Detainers\nL5@P0: (Evictions)\nL6@P0: UPDATE – Friday, September 23, 2024\nL7@P0: In-person services are available in the Civil Clerk’s Office Monday through Friday from 8:00 a.m. to 4:00\nL8@P0: p.m.\nL9@P0: 1. Filings: Unlawful detainer filings shall be submitted via eFiling through an approved eFiling Service\nL10@P0: Provider with the exception of filings by self-represented litigants. Self-represented litigants may\nL11@P0: submit filings in person at the Central Justice Center, via electronic filing, or by US Mail at 700 Civic\nL12@P0: Center Drive West, Santa Ana, CA 92701.\nL13@P0: 2. Questions: Specific questions can be submitted via the “Ask a Question” button on the court’s\nL14@P0: website.\nL15@P0: 3. Self Help Assistance- The public is encouraged to consult Self Help Services prior to filing\nL16@P0: documents. To contact Self Help, visit www.occourts.org/self-help and select \"Click Here to Contact\nL17@P0: Self Help Services\".\nL18@P0: 4. Appearances (Departments C17 and C61):\nL19@P0: The Court will offer remote appearances for all law and motion, case management conferences,\nL20@P0: status conferences, ex partes, and other non-evidentiary proceedings. Trials and evidentiary\nL21@P0: hearings will be held in person.\nL22@P0: Remote appearance will be conducted via Zoom through the video links available on the court’s\nL23@P0: Civil Appearance Procedure and Information page. Click on the blue bar as displayed below to\nL24@P0: access the video link for the courtroom where the hearing is set.\nL25@P0: To view Remote Hearing Instructions click here or visit https://www.occourts.org/media\u0002relations/covid/CivilPublicRemoteHearingInstructionsZoom.pdf.\nL26@P0: In the event a party, witness, official reporter, official reporter pro tempore, court interpreter, or\nL27@P0: other court personnel experiences technology or audibility issues that arise during a remote\nL28@P0: conference, hearing, proceeding, or trial, the person is to alert the court by calling the\nL29@P0: courtroom. Phone numbers for the courtrooms can be found at\nL30@P0: https://www.occourts.org/directory/civil/CivilPhoneDepartmentDirectory.pdf.\nL31@P0: Parties should review Local Rule 375 (https://www.occourts.org/directory/local\u0002rules/2022/Div3.pdf) for additional appearance information.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMicrosoft Word - Restraining_Order_Information_and_Video_Appearance_Process (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/civil/restraining_order_appearance_procedure_and_information_09_24.pdf)\nciteturn1024view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 2; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn997view0\",\"id\":321}); Total lines: 43\nL0@P0: 1 | P a g e\nL1@P0: Superior Court of California\nL2@P0: County of Orange\nL3@P0: Appearance Procedure and Information\nL4@P0: Civil - Restraining Orders (Including Civil\nL5@P0: Harassment, Gun Violence Restraining\nL6@P0: Orders, Workplace Violence, School Site\nL7@P0: Violence, Transitional Housing Misconduct)\nL8@P0: UPDATE – Friday, September 24, 2024\nL9@P0: In-person services are available in the Civil Clerk’s Office Monday through Friday from 8:00 a.m. to 4:00\nL10@P0: p.m.\nL11@P0: 1. Filings: Filings may be submitted in-person at the Central Justice Center, via eFiling through an\nL12@P0: approved eFiling Service Provider, or by US Mail at 700 Civic Center Drive West, Santa Ana, CA\nL13@P0: 92701.\nL14@P0: 2. Questions: Specific questions can be submitted via the “Ask a Question” button on the court’s\nL15@P0: website.\nL16@P0: 3. Self Help Assistance: The public is encouraged to consult Self Help Services prior to filing\nL17@P0: documents. To contact Self Help, visit www.occourts.org/self-help and select \"Click Here to Contact\nL18@P0: Self Help Services\".\nL19@P0: Additional information regarding restraining orders can be found on the court’s website at\nL20@P0: http://www.occourts.org/self-help/restrainingorders and https://california.tylerhost.net/SRL.\nL21@P0: 4. Law enforcement emergency Gun Violence Restraining Order (GVRO) requests will continue to\nL22@P0: be processed via the on-call EPO Referee procedure.\nL23@P0: 5. Appearances (Departments C64 and C65):\nL24@P0: Ex parte requests for temporary restraining orders will be ruled on the papers without hearing\nL25@P0: for civil harassment, workplace violence, school site violence, and transitional housing\nL26@P0: misconduct. The Court will offer remote appearances for all other non-evidentiary proceedings\nL27@P0: for these case types. Trials and evidentiary hearings will be held in person.\nL28@P0: Remote appearance will be conducted via Zoom through the video links available on the court’s\nL29@P0: Civil Appearance Procedure and Information page. Click on the blue bar as displayed below to\nL30@P0: access the video link for the courtroom where the hearing is set.\nL31@P0-1: To view Remote Hearing Instructions click here or visit https://www.occourts.org/media\u0002relations/covid/CivilPublicRemoteHearingInstructionsZoom.pdf.2 | P a g e\nL32@P1: In the event a party, witness, official reporter, official reporter pro tempore, court interpreter, or\nL33@P1: other court personnel experiences technology or audibility issues that arise during a remote\nL34@P1: conference, hearing, proceeding, or trial, the person is to alert the court by calling the courtroom.\nL35@P1: Phone numbers for the courtrooms can be found at\nL36@P1: https://www.occourts.org/directory/civil/CivilPhoneDepartmentDirectory.pdf.\nL37@P1: Parties should review Local Rule 375 (https://www.occourts.org/directory/local\u0002rules/2022/Div3.pdf) for additional appearance information.\nL38@P1: 6. Gun Violence Restraining Orders (Department C61):\nL39@P1: Pursuant to Penal Code section 18123(a), a party or witness may appear remotely at the\nL40@P1: hearing on a petition for a gun violence restraining order. Parties shall provide notice of remote\nL41@P1: appearance to the Court online by clicking on a court-provided hyperlink and agreeing to the\nL42@P1: remote appearance.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGuidelines for remote appearances (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/general/guidelinesforremoteproceedings9-7-22.pdf)\nciteturn1024view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 2; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn997view0\",\"id\":328}); Total lines: 49\nL0@P0: Superior Court of California\nL1@P0: County of Orange\nL2@P0: GUIDELINES FOR REMOTE APPEARANCES\nL3@P0: Please bear in mind that remote proceedings are official court proceedings. All participants must\nL4@P0: maintain appropriate demeanor and decorum at all times.\nL5@P0: Inability or failure to participate appropriately via remote may result in the hearing being continued\nL6@P0: to an in-person hearing.\nL7@P0: These guidelines are not intended to supersede specific policies/procedures adopted by individual\nL8@P0: Departments.\nL9@P0: Preparing for the Remote Appearance\nL10@P0: 1. Participants must wear appropriate courtroom attire for all appearances.\nL11@P0: 2. Participants must be in a private, quiet location, without disruptions or distractions. Cell\nL12@P0: phones must be on silent mode and may not be viewed or used during the session.\nL13@P0: 3. Participants’ cameras must be positioned to assure their face is fully visible.\nL14@P0: 4. Participants should consider what is visible in the background of their remote meeting location.\nL15@P0: 5. Participants may consider using headphones to reduce feedback and improve audio quality.\nL16@P0: 6. Participants should test their cameras and audio in advance of the hearing.\nL17@P0: 7. Participants may not appear from a moving vehicle and may not eat or drink during the\nL18@P0: proceeding.\nL19@P0: 8. Any form of recording of the proceeding is strictly prohibited.\nL20@P0: Checking In\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMicrosoft Word - Civil_Limited_Unlimited_Complex_Information_Appearance_Process (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/civil/civil_unlimited_and_complex_appearance_procedure_and_information.pdf)\nciteturn1024view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 2; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn997view0\",\"id\":329}); Total lines: 36\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSuperior Court of California County of Orange (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/civil/appearanceproceduresandinformation-civillimiteddepartmentcx105.pdf)\nciteturn1024view6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 2; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn997view0\",\"id\":330}); Total lines: 65\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSuperior Court of California County of Orange (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/general/probate_mental_health_information_and_appearance_process_2024.pdf)\nciteturn1024view7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn997view2\",\"id\":319}); Total lines: 34\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSuperior Court of California County of Orange (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/general/appearance_procedure_and_information-appellate_division.pdf)\nciteturn1024view8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 2; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn997view1\",\"id\":320}); Total lines: 70\n"
